  "ai_show_review": {
    "summary": "Relaxed ’69 set with stellar Morning Dew, first Easy Wind & tight jam",
    "blurb": "The band delivers a laid‑back performance highlighted by beautiful vocals on Doin' That Rag and an inspired early rendition of Easy Wind. Standout moments include Morning Dew, the brief but bright Dark Star, and a unique China Cat Sunflower with guest flute. The soundboard capture is clear and well‑balanced, making this show a pleasant listen.",
    "review": "On August 21, 1969 at Seattle’s Aqua Theatre the Dead unfolded a mellow, psychedelic set that feels like a snapshot of their post‑Woodstock experimentation. Jerry’s voice shines throughout – especially on Doin' That Rag – and his guitar work is crisp, while the rhythm section of Bill Kreutzmann and Mickey Hart provides a smooth, cohesive foundation. Highlights abound: a heartfelt Morning Dew, the first-ever performance of Easy Wind that adds a fresh country‑flavored touch, a concise but sparkling Dark Star, and an unforgettable China Cat Sunflower embellished by a guest flautist. The second‑half jam sequence – The Other One → Dark Star → Cosmic Charlie – flows with relaxed improvisation, showcasing the band’s ability to wander without losing direction. Captured on a good‑quality soundboard, the mix balances guitars, vocals and the added flute beautifully despite a touch of tape hiss, offering an enjoyable listening experience for both completists and casual fans.",
